Model weights
-------------
models/nemo8.tnm contains weights derived from NVIDIA's "stt_en_conformer_ctc_small" (NVIDIA NeMo), licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.
Changes: re-implemented in PyTorch (train/nemo_small.py), quantized to int8 and packed into the TNM1 format
(train/export_nemo.py). models/nemo_small/tokenizer.model is the model's original SentencePiece tokenizer. nemo8.tnm
and the tokenizer remain available under CC-BY-4.0.

models/nemo4.tnm is the same NVIDIA model, fine-tuned by Lokutor with 4-bit quantization-aware training (8,000 steps)
on public speech corpora and quantized to int4. Fine-tuning data:
- Common Voice 17 (CC0) and VoxPopuli (CC0);
- LibriSpeech and Multilingual LibriSpeech English (CC-BY-4.0);
- AMI and VCTK (CC-BY-4.0);
- People's Speech, with transcripts regenerated by NVIDIA parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2 (CC-BY / CC-BY-SA);
- OpenSLR 70 and 83 (CC-BY-SA-4.0).
Because of the share-alike sources, nemo4.tnm is released under CC-BY-SA-4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/.

models/nemo_lm.tlm is a GRU language model (1.3 M parameters) trained by Lokutor on the LibriSpeech language-modeling
corpus (public domain text from 14,500 books, https://www.openslr.org/11/), over the vocabulary of NVIDIA's tokenizer. It
is released under CC-BY-4.0.

NVIDIA's "stt_en_conformer_transducer_small" is supported by the engine but not included; it is distributed by NVIDIA
on NGC under the NGC Terms of Use.

Data used for evaluation (not redistributed)
--------------------------------------------
LibriSpeech (CC-BY-4.0), DEMAND noise corpus (CC-BY-4.0, used by eval/make_robust.py).
